# Oakfern line-endings policy.
#
# `.prettierrc` sets `endOfLine: "lf"`, so `prettier --check .` — half of `pnpm lint` —
# fails on any file checked out with CRLF. On Windows with `core.autocrlf=true` that was
# every text file in the repository, which made `pnpm lint` impossible to pass locally and
# every task's `Verify: pnpm lint` unprovable. These rules make LF the one true line ending
# in the index *and* in the working tree on every platform, independent of local git config.

# Normalise every text file to LF in the index and check it out as LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touch their bytes, never diff them as text.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.pdf  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.eot   binary

# SVG is text (we hand-edit it) but must stay LF like everything else.
*.svg text eol=lf

# Lockfiles are text but generated; keep them LF and out of diffs.
pnpm-lock.yaml text eol=lf -diff
